From 2b1522226cf61179b7bd3af7486d7cdf90a626ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:44:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: validate fetchmany(size) before fetching rows

fetchmany() used `size` as-is: a float such as 2.5 failed deep inside
the row loop with a bare `TypeError: slice indices must be integers`,
and a zero or negative size silently returned an empty list that is
easy to mistake for "no more rows".

Validate `size` up front, the same way as the `arraysize` setter (an
int >= 1), with a shared `validate_fetch_size()` helper in
`_cursor_common` used by both the sync and async cursors. A non-int
(float, str, bool), zero or negative size now raises ProgrammingError
before any rows are consumed. `fetchmany()` without arguments still
uses `arraysize`.

Closes #371
